From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 12:17:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] chore(fork): add integration patch-management system on
 pinned v1.4.0 baseline
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Mirrors the patches workflow used in gastown/beads, adapted for gascity:

- integration branch = pinned BASELINE (an upstream release tag, currently
  v1.4.0, pinned by SHA) + fork patches; deliberately NOT main.
- make patches       — export BASELINE..HEAD divergence to patches/,
  excluding patches/ itself (no recursive self-inclusion).
- make upgrade       — reset integration to BASELINE and replay patches via
  git am --3way (scripts/upgrade-integration.sh); copies patches/ to a tmpdir
  before the reset since the baseline does not track it, then regenerates.
- make check-patches — fail if patches/ drifts from the divergence; wired into
  the integration-branch pre-push as validation-only (never amends).
- BASELINE_VERSION stamps fork builds as 1.4.0-integration so gc version proves
  the LTS lineage instead of reporting dev/main.

The baseline SHA lives only in the Makefile and the upgrade script's default,
never in this message, so bumping it does not leave a stale SHA behind here.

Workflow: engdocs/contributors/fork-patches.md

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
